Sure! Here’s a simple setup for your Node.js web server using the Express framework:

1. First, install Express if you haven't already:
   ```bash
   npm install express
   ```

2. Create a file named `server.js` and add the following code:
   ```javascript
   const express = require('express');
   const app = express();
   const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

   app.get('/', (req, res) => {
       res.send('Hello World!');
   });

   app.listen(PORT, () => {
       console.log(`Server is running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
   });
   ```

3. Run your server:
   ```bash
   node server.js
   ```

